From cff84aabce176446f307fe4df5e95581297aebcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexanderNyr <131390634+AlexanderNyr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 11:48:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] W7 update: <canvas> with OpenGL

WEBVIEW_PLAN.md phase W7:
- wv_canvas.{h,c}: the only web-view module that includes GL headers;
  <canvas data-scene="cube"> renders the built-in cube scene into an
  FBO (G12) and is composited into the page like any other box
- GL is NOT on the paint critical path: one-shot render at page load
  into a cached buffer; repaint only blits (clipped, scrolled with the
  page); a page without a canvas never touches libgl (the W4 reference
  hash 0x4D394D5C is unchanged)
- measured cost: 64x48 cube in ~58 us host / sub-tick in QEMU TCG --
  the number the plan's section 1 table was missing
- host gate: test_wv_canvas.c 21 checks (real wv_canvas.c vs real
  libgl): cube faces visible, two renders byte-identical, invalid
  sizes refused, blit clipping (placement/scroll/off-screen/edges),
  2000 fuzz blits
- QEMU gate: canvas smoke: PASS (hash 4d394d5c -> 8a6c0574);
  test_webview_net gained /canvas.html (text + cube) and asserts
  'canvas: rendered 64x48 cube'; 15 + 13 assertions, all green
- no JavaScript (D5): a page can only ask for a scene
- webview.elf ~374 KB (libgl +186 KB) - inside SPAWN_MAX_IMAGE
